---
/**
 * CaseStudies.astro — Proof, Not Promises
 * Two case study cards showcasing real client and own-brand results.
 * Grid layout: details left (60%), results right (40%) on desktop.
 */
---

<section id="results" class="pb-8 pt-24 md:pt-32">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <!-- Section Heading -->
    <h2
      class="mb-16 text-center text-3xl font-bold md:text-4xl"
      style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; letter-spacing: -0.025em;"
    >
      <span class="comment-prefix">// </span><span class="gradient-text">Proof, Not Promises</span>
    </h2>

    <!-- Cards Container -->
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-8">

      {/* Client case study — anonymised: figures yes, names never */}
      <div
        class="fade-in-up glass-card overflow-hidden p-8 md:p-10"
      >
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 md:grid-cols-[3fr_2fr] md:gap-10">
          <!-- Left: Details -->
          <div>
            <!-- Tag -->
            <span
              class="mb-4 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs"
              style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; background-color: rgba(240, 96, 0, 0.1); color: #f06000;"
            >
              Client Project
            </span>

            <!-- Title -->
            <h3
              class="mb-4 text-xl font-bold md:text-2xl"
              style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
            >
              Traditional Retail Shop to Full E-Commerce Operation
            </h3>

            <!-- Challenge -->
            <p
              class="mb-6 leading-relaxed"
              style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;"
            >
              New owner, one week into a long-established specialty retail business. Zero e-commerce experience. Working 84+ hours a week. Needed a complete digital transformation plan — fast.
            </p>

            <!-- What I built -->
            <h4
              class="mb-3 text-base font-semibold"
              style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #ffffff;"
            >
              What I built
            </h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span>18 deliverable areas — competitive analysis, pricing strategy, SEO, email, social, UGC, partnerships, financial tracking</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span>Custom Content Creator PRO v5.3 — web app for generating platform-specific AI prompts, handed over running</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span>Corporate gifting program with B2B sales materials — a six-figure channel that didn't exist before</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span>Pricing optimization strategy — a six-figure annual gain from margin adjustments alone</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span>Interactive client dashboard deployed on GitHub Pages — live, browser-based, no downloads</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Right: Results -->
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 md:border-l md:pl-10" style="border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);">
            <div>
              <div
                class="text-3xl font-bold"
                style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
              >
                6 Weeks
              </div>
              <div class="text-sm" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
                Delivery Time
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div
                class="text-3xl font-bold"
                style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
              >
                Six Figures
              </div>
              <div class="text-sm" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
                Added From Pricing Alone
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div
                class="text-3xl font-bold"
                style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
              >
                New Channel
              </div>
              <div class="text-sm" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
                Corporate Gifting, Built From Zero
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div
                class="text-3xl font-bold"
                style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
              >
                ~2×
              </div>
              <div class="text-sm" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
                Revenue Trajectory
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* Own-build portfolio. Replaced an auto-shop client case study on
          2026-08-02: that project was a first trial done for family, it is
          being handed over, and there was nothing shippable to point at.

          This card carries the range argument the auto shop used to carry, but
          it does it differently — the client card above answers "has he done
          this for someone like me", this one answers "can he actually build at
          this level". Keep both. Cutting either leaves an obvious hole.

          FRAMING — do not undo this. The card is about SPEED, not headcount.
          Greg's point (2026-08-02) is that every change used to require going
          to a developer and waiting days; now he makes it himself, often from
          his phone, and it is live immediately. That is the thing clients
          actually buy, and it is a pain every business owner has felt.

          Never write "I fired my developers" or any variant. Same underlying
          fact, but an owner reads it as "this man replaces people" — and it
          contradicts the position taken at the Oakville meetup, where the
          honest answer is that AI replaced the agency, not the staff.

          Client work stays visible here on purpose. Greg was explicit that
          client builds should not be discarded in favour of own-brand work;
          saying "built for a client" is fine.
          Anonymisation still applies: Astro renders <!-- --> into the HTML,
          {/* */} it does not. The build gate fails on a client name either way. */}
      <div
        class="fade-in-up glass-card overflow-hidden p-8 md:p-10"
      >
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 md:grid-cols-[3fr_2fr] md:gap-10">
          <!-- Left: Details -->
          <div>
            <!-- Tag -->
            <span
              class="mb-4 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs"
              style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; background-color: rgba(240, 96, 0, 0.1); color: #f06000;"
            >
              Built Without Waiting
            </span>

            <!-- Title -->
            <h3
              class="mb-4 text-xl font-bold md:text-2xl"
              style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
            >
              It Used to Take Days. Now I Do It From My Phone.
            </h3>

            <!-- Challenge -->
            <p
              class="mb-4 leading-relaxed"
              style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;"
            >
              Every change used to mean going to a developer. A blog post, a price update, a page that needed fixing — write the brief, wait, review it, wait again. Days, every time, for work that took minutes to describe. And nothing shipped while you waited.
            </p>

            <p
              class="mb-6 leading-relaxed"
              style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;"
            >
              That's the part that changed. I make the change myself now, often from my phone, and it's live before the conversation is over. Not because I became a programmer — I'm a mechanical engineer and I've never written software professionally. Because describing the work precisely is now enough to get it built.
            </p>

            <!-- What I built -->
            <h4
              class="mb-3 text-base font-semibold"
              style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #ffffff;"
            >
              What's been shipped that way
            </h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span><strong style="color: #ffffff;">Two iOS apps, live in the App Store</strong> — SunUp, which calculates real burn time from skin type and live UV, and RunMate Pro, GPS tracking with shoe-mileage management. RunMate was rejected 39 times before it was approved.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span><strong style="color: #ffffff;">Helm</strong> — seller intelligence that pulls Amazon SP-API, Amazon Ads, Shopify, Meta, Klaviyo and Search Console into one place, then exposes it to Claude as tools. "Why did ACOS jump last week" gets answered in a sentence instead of an afternoon.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span><strong style="color: #ffffff;">A full event platform</strong> for a chip-timed road race I direct — over a thousand people involved across runners, families and spectators, plus what that brings into the local economy. Registration, course and festival info, sponsor pages, and a permanent searchable photo archive.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span><strong style="color: #ffffff;">Two Shopify stores</strong> running on API connections, with product content and blog production automated end to end.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span><strong style="color: #ffffff;">SportsClinicFinder</strong> — a Canada-wide clinic directory covering every province and territory, searchable by city, injury, and specialty.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span><strong style="color: #ffffff;">Magpie</strong> — a shared research brain for the team. Drop in a link and it enriches, categorises, and makes it searchable across every brand, so nobody researches the same thing twice.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span><strong style="color: #ffffff;">Marketing sites for both apps</strong>, plus this one — statically built, deployed on Vercel, with a post-build audit that fails the deploy on a dead link or a broken image.</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span><strong style="color: #ffffff;">Content Creator PRO — built for a client</strong>, handed over running. A web app that produces on-brand content for Instagram, email, Google Ads and product pages, so they stopped needing an agency on retainer to do it.</span>
              </li>
            </ul>

            <p
              class="mt-6 leading-relaxed"
              style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;"
            >
              This is the same capability I hand over. When a client wants a page changed, a post published, or a price updated, the answer stops being "I'll ask the developer and get back to you next week."
            </p>
            <a
              href="/projects/"
              class="mt-6 inline-block text-sm font-semibold transition-opacity hover:opacity-70"
              style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #f06000;"
            >See all of it, with the stack behind each one →</a>
          </div>

          <!-- Right: Results -->
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 md:border-l md:pl-10" style="border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);">
            <div>
              <div
                class="text-3xl font-bold"
                style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
              >
                Minutes
              </div>
              <div class="text-sm" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
                To Ship a Change — Not Days
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div
                class="text-3xl font-bold"
                style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
              >
                2 Apps
              </div>
              <div class="text-sm" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
                Live in the App Store
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div
                class="text-3xl font-bold"
                style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
              >
                12
              </div>
              <div class="text-sm" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
                Projects Shipped
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div
                class="text-3xl font-bold"
                style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
              >
                $75K+
              </div>
              <div class="text-sm" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
                Annual Agency Cost Removed
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* Own brands — GearTOP + TapeGeeks, safe to name */}
      <div
        class="fade-in-up glass-card overflow-hidden p-8 md:p-10"
      >
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 md:grid-cols-[3fr_2fr] md:gap-10">
          <!-- Left: Details -->
          <div>
            <!-- Tag -->
            <span
              class="mb-4 inline-block rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs"
              style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; background-color: rgba(240, 96, 0, 0.1); color: #f06000;"
            >
              My Businesses
            </span>

            <!-- Title -->
            <h3
              class="mb-4 text-xl font-bold md:text-2xl"
              style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
            >
              Two E-Commerce Brands Running on AI Tools I Built Myself
            </h3>

            <!-- Challenge -->
            <p
              class="mb-6 leading-relaxed"
              style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;"
            >
              Two e-commerce brands. $2M+ in ad spend. Paying $75K-$125K annually for agencies, freelancers, and services. Needed to cut costs without cutting results.
            </p>

            <!-- What I built -->
            <h4
              class="mb-3 text-base font-semibold"
              style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #ffffff;"
            >
              What I built
            </h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span>Custom AI content generation systems (100+ product descriptions, brand voice maintained)</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span>Marketing automation workflows replacing manual email, social, and ad management</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span>2 iOS apps (SunUp by GearTOP, RunMate Pro) — built as a non-coder using AI tools</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span>Analytics dashboards aggregating data from Shopify, Amazon, Google, Meta</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full" style="background-color: #f06000;"></span>
                <span>Operational automation (inventory alerts, reorder triggers, journey orchestration)</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Right: Results -->
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 md:border-l md:pl-10" style="border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);">
            <div>
              <div
                class="text-3xl font-bold"
                style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
              >
                $75K+
              </div>
              <div class="text-sm" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
                Annual Savings
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div
                class="text-3xl font-bold"
                style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
              >
                5-10x
              </div>
              <div class="text-sm" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
                Content Volume
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div
                class="text-3xl font-bold"
                style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
              >
                15-20x
              </div>
              <div class="text-sm" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
                Email Marketing ROI
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div
                class="text-3xl font-bold"
                style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; color: #ffffff;"
              >
                2 Apps
              </div>
              <div class="text-sm" style="font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; color: #798897;">
                Live in App Store
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
